</p><p>Real GDP per head is estimated to have increased by 0.6% in Quarter 1 2026, and is up by 0.7% compared with the same quarter a year ago. See <a href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/grossdomesticproductgdp/bulletins/quarterlynationalaccounts/januarytomarch2026#real-gdp-per-head-and-real-household-disposable-income-per-head">Section 6: Real GDP per head and real household disposable income per head</a> for more information.</p><p>
<div class="markdown-table-container print--avoid-break">
    <div class="scrollable-container" tabindex="0">
        <div class="markdown-table-wrap">
            <figure class="figure" id="table-eda16b21">
<table class="table">
