</p><p>We estimate real household disposable income (RHDI) per head by dividing RHDI by the total UK population. RHDI per head has decreased by 0.8% in Quarter 1 2026, following an increase of 1.2% in the previous quarter. The components of this measure are further broken down in <a href="https://www.ons.gov.uk/economy/grossdomesticproductgdp/bulletins/quarterlynationalaccounts/januarytomarch2026#quarterly-sector-accounts">Section 7: Quarterly sector accounts</a> of this bulletin. </p><p>


  

    <div class="markdown-chart-container panel--bottom-mar print--avoid-break">

      <h3 class="flush--third--vertical font-size--18 padding-top--0 margin-bottom--1">Figure 10: Real household disposable income per head is estimated to have decreased by 0.8% in Quarter 1 2026, from an increase of 1.2% in Quarter 4 2025 </h3>
        
            <h4 class="flush--third--bottom font-size--16 padding-top--0 margin-top--0">UK, real household disposable income per head, seasonally adjusted, Quarter 1 (Jan to Mar) 2024 to Quarter 1 2026</h4>
        

      <div class="scrollable-container">
        <div id="chart-5c1ba79d" data-filename="5c1ba79d" data-uri="/economy/grossdomesticproductgdp/bulletins/quarterlynationalaccounts/januarytomarch2026/5c1ba79d" class="markdown-chart">
            <!--[if gt IE 8]><!--><noscript><!--[endif]-->
